# API proxy & security

## Golden rules

1. **Browser never calls `API_BASE_URL`** — only `/api/proxy/*` via `axiosClient`
2. **`API_BASE_URL` is server-only** — `getServerApiBaseUrl()` in Route Handlers, Server Actions, `createServerAxios()`
3. **Tokens in HttpOnly cookies** — `access_token`, `refresh_token` (`src/lib/constants.ts`); do not persist tokens in Zustand/localStorage

## Client HTTP

```ts
// ✅ Client components, SWR fetcher, apis/*
import { axiosClient } from '@/lib/axios-client'; // baseURL: /api/proxy

// ❌ Never in client code
axios.get(process.env.API_BASE_URL + '/users');
```

## Proxy route

- Entry: `src/app/api/proxy/[...path]/route.ts` → `proxyRequest()` / `handleMockProxy()` when `USE_MOCK_API=true`
- Forward `Authorization` from cookies; handle 401 refresh server-side in `api-proxy.ts`

## Auth routes

- `/api/auth/login`, `logout`, `refresh` — set/clear cookies via `src/features/auth/actions.ts`
- After login: update Zustand `user` from response body only (not access token)

## Adding endpoints

1. Add mock branch in `mock-proxy.ts` if using mock mode
2. Add `swrKeys` / `apis/*` path relative to proxy root (e.g. `/products` → `/api/proxy/products`)
3. Document new env vars in `.env.example`
